.TH "CUSTODIAN-CODEX" "1" "" "Custodian" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
custodian-codex \- Install and operate Custodian Codex Guard: fail\-closed tool\-call enforcement, action\-bound approvals, and authenticated receipts.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B custodian-codex
[OPTIONS] COMMAND [ARGS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Install and operate Custodian Codex Guard: fail\-closed tool\-call enforcement, action\-bound approvals, and authenticated receipts.
.SH COMMAND REFERENCE
.SS custodian\-codex
.nf
usage: custodian\-codex [\-h]
                       {setup,hook\-uninstall,disable,paladin\-git,approve,deny,status,doctor} ...

Install and operate Custodian Codex Guard: fail\-closed tool\-call enforcement, action\-bound approvals, and authenticated receipts.

positional arguments:
  {setup,hook\-uninstall,disable,paladin\-git,approve,deny,status,doctor}
    setup               install the plugin, MCP server, and enforcement hook
    hook\-uninstall      operator escape hatch: remove the enforcement hook
    disable             operator escape hatch; preserve evidence
    paladin\-git         wire git \-> Paladin for one host so Codex resolves tokens from the vault
    approve             approve one exact pending action
    deny                headless denial of a pending approval
    status              verify receipts and show approval counts
    doctor              check the local Codex Guard installation

options:
  \-h, \-\-help            show this help message and exit

examples:
  custodian\-codex setup
  custodian\-codex doctor
  custodian\-codex approve latest
  custodian\-codex status

Run `custodian\-codex COMMAND \-\-help` for command\-specific options.
.fi
.SS custodian\-codex setup
.nf
usage: custodian\-codex setup [\-h] [\-\-dry\-run] [\-\-matcher MATCHER] [\-\-managed\-lock]

options:
  \-h, \-\-help         show this help message and exit
  \-\-dry\-run          show the installation actions without changing the system
  \-\-matcher MATCHER  tool\-name regex the hook governs (default '.*' = all tools)
  \-\-managed\-lock     also install an always\-on managed hook and lock config to managed hooks only
                     (needs root/managed\-dir write)
.fi
.SS custodian\-codex hook\-uninstall
.nf
usage: custodian\-codex hook\-uninstall [\-h] [\-\-managed]

options:
  \-h, \-\-help  show this help message and exit
  \-\-managed   remove the always\-on MANAGED hook + lock (needs root/admin write to the managed dir)
.fi
.SS custodian\-codex disable
.nf
usage: custodian\-codex disable [\-h]

options:
  \-h, \-\-help  show this help message and exit
.fi
.SS custodian\-codex paladin\-git
.nf
usage: custodian\-codex paladin\-git [\-h] host ref

positional arguments:
  host        git host, e.g. github.com
  ref         vault ref name to resolve for that host

options:
  \-h, \-\-help  show this help message and exit
.fi
.SS custodian\-codex approve
.nf
usage: custodian\-codex approve [\-h] [\-\-digest DIGEST] [\-\-operator OPERATOR] approval_id

positional arguments:
  approval_id          approval UUID, or 'latest'

options:
  \-h, \-\-help           show this help message and exit
  \-\-digest DIGEST      optional full digest copied from Guard for independent verification
  \-\-operator OPERATOR  operator identity (defaults to USER or USERNAME)
.fi
.SS custodian\-codex deny
.nf
usage: custodian\-codex deny [\-h] [\-\-operator OPERATOR] approval_id

positional arguments:
  approval_id          approval UUID, or 'latest'

options:
  \-h, \-\-help           show this help message and exit
  \-\-operator OPERATOR  operator identity (falls back to $USER)
.fi
.SS custodian\-codex status
.nf
usage: custodian\-codex status [\-h]

options:
  \-h, \-\-help  show this help message and exit
.fi
.SS custodian\-codex doctor
.nf
usage: custodian\-codex doctor [\-h]

options:
  \-h, \-\-help  show this help message and exit
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR custodian (1),
.BR custodian-codex (1)
